WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.167 --> 00:00:04.046
We are bringing another girl
on to the brokerage.

00:00:04.129 --> 00:00:06.006
-Really?
-Yeah. Chrishell.

00:00:06.089 --> 00:00:08.217
Chrishell, okay.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:12.137
I really put a lot of focus
on my career.

00:00:12.221 --> 00:00:14.473
So now I definitely
would say

00:00:14.556 --> 00:00:15.807
I'm one of
the top selling agents

00:00:15.891 --> 00:00:16.725
at the Oppenheim Group

00:00:16.808 --> 00:00:20.270
and I worked really hard
and I'm finally in a place

00:00:20.354 --> 00:00:21.647
to buy my own house.

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:24.066
So it's definitely
looking up.

00:00:26.944 --> 00:00:28.612
Oh my god.

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:30.864
It's all ready for you
to decorate, Amanza.

00:00:30.948 --> 00:00:33.075
What do you guys think?

00:00:34.493 --> 00:00:35.369
I love it.

00:00:35.452 --> 00:00:38.080
I am so happy for you.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:46.797
-Hi. You're welcome.
-Hi.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.007
-Hi, how are you? Good.
-I'm good. How are you?

00:00:49.091 --> 00:00:50.467
You're welcome.

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:52.636
Oh, you're so cute.

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:54.054
Hi, cutie.

00:00:54.137 --> 00:00:55.472
Can I give this to you?

00:00:55.556 --> 00:00:56.682
Thank you.

00:00:56.765 --> 00:00:58.517
Here you go.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:00:59.726
I think there's
a huge stigma

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:02.813
with growing up
in poverty or,

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:04.022
you know, being homeless.

00:01:04.106 --> 00:01:06.149
I mean, I think these
charities are important.

00:01:06.233 --> 00:01:07.985
Because
when you treat people

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:10.195
in a bad situation
with respect,

00:01:10.279 --> 00:01:13.073
that's when they
really feel uplifted

00:01:13.156 --> 00:01:15.659
and maybe they can garner
some change in their life.

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:17.786
It's a moving thing
to be a part of.

00:01:17.870 --> 00:01:20.205
-Thank you guys.
-It's awesome.

00:01:20.789 --> 00:01:23.208
It was honestly so nice,
being here and you know,

00:01:23.292 --> 00:01:25.210
just smile to people
and make eye contact

00:01:25.294 --> 00:01:26.378
and give them--

00:01:26.461 --> 00:01:28.046
That's what like, for me,

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:30.883
like our family was one of
the families in that line.

00:01:30.966 --> 00:01:33.927
So it's been like
so gratifying to be here,

00:01:34.011 --> 00:01:35.554
but also like,
it's hard to like--

00:01:35.637 --> 00:01:37.055
-A little emotional?
-A little emotional.

00:01:37.139 --> 00:01:39.308
Just because it's like,
when you see that boy.

00:01:39.391 --> 00:01:41.685
It's like I remember
being in that line so,

00:01:42.519 --> 00:01:43.854
I'm so happy
that you guys did this.

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:45.689
I'm sorry,
I'm such a mess today.

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:52.321
I feel like, at that dinner
you conveniently--

00:01:52.404 --> 00:01:53.906
This isn't about making
points right now.

00:01:53.989 --> 00:01:56.116
Can you stop.
I'm trying to make--

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:57.576
I know, but you made
your point. Trust me.

00:01:57.659 --> 00:02:00.162
Can I reiterate
and you get off my back?

00:02:01.038 --> 00:02:02.915
I always own up to my stuff.

00:02:02.998 --> 00:02:04.208
If, in the moment,

00:02:04.291 --> 00:02:06.502
I didn't know exactly
what she was talking about.

00:02:06.585 --> 00:02:08.170
Now,
I've already talked to Mary.

00:02:08.253 --> 00:02:09.421
I've told her
everything I said.

00:02:09.505 --> 00:02:11.256
I own up
to everything I said.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:12.174
I understand that.

00:02:12.257 --> 00:02:14.510
But we came back from
the bathroom Maya and I

00:02:14.593 --> 00:02:17.095
and we had asked you what
you guys were talking about

00:02:17.179 --> 00:02:18.680
and you said
"I don't remember.

00:02:18.764 --> 00:02:20.432
I just said stuff about
Mary and Romain."

00:02:20.516 --> 00:02:22.476
Christine, I'm not gonna
have this conversation.

00:02:22.559 --> 00:02:24.311
Because you know
that I'm right.

00:02:24.394 --> 00:02:25.354
Christine, here's the thing.

00:02:25.437 --> 00:02:26.980
You said you don't remember.

00:02:27.064 --> 00:02:29.066
It makes you sound
like you're two-faced.

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:31.318
Also, I don't have to
tell you what I said.

00:02:31.401 --> 00:02:33.820
Also, it makes you sound
like you're two-faced

00:02:33.904 --> 00:02:36.865
when you don't own up
to the shit that you say.

00:02:36.949 --> 00:02:38.367
Do you understand
where I'm coming from?

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:40.577
When I ask you
what did you say.

00:02:40.661 --> 00:02:42.871
-When I ask you--
-Don't yell at me.

00:02:42.955 --> 00:02:44.122
-what did you say.
-Okay, hold on.

00:02:44.206 --> 00:02:46.750
And you don't own up
to what you said,

00:02:46.834 --> 00:02:48.502
it makes you look like
a crazy person.

00:02:48.585 --> 00:02:51.004
If you keep yelling at me
I'm not gonna listen to you.

00:02:51.088 --> 00:02:53.298
I always own up
to what I say.

00:02:53.382 --> 00:02:55.050
I say "Yeah,
I've said this, so what?

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:56.468
Yeah, I've said it,
I'll back it up."

00:02:56.552 --> 00:02:58.679
I've talked to Mary
about what I've said.

00:02:58.762 --> 00:03:01.223
But when I asked you
at the dinner,

00:03:01.306 --> 00:03:03.058
you conveniently
didn't remember.

00:03:03.141 --> 00:03:05.102
You understand the
difference, right.

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:06.270
Or do you
still have dementia?

00:03:07.145 --> 00:03:10.357
Christine.
Leave everything behind.

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.651
I mean come one. Yeah, no
rebuttal because I'm right.

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:17.364
Christine, this is enough.

00:03:17.447 --> 00:03:18.866
-I'm leaving.
-Seriously?

00:03:18.949 --> 00:03:20.617
Don't do this again to me.

00:03:21.368 --> 00:03:23.287
We had a fight that morning
over the phone

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:25.747
and I never saw him since.

00:03:25.831 --> 00:03:27.541
We didn't talk
things through and…

00:03:28.917 --> 00:03:31.503
before we had a chance
to figure anything out

00:03:31.587 --> 00:03:32.629
he'd filed.

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:43.223
How did you find out?

00:03:43.307 --> 00:03:44.933
Did he like just
come talk to you

00:03:45.017 --> 00:03:46.435
out of the blue or what?

00:03:52.941 --> 00:03:56.695
I found out
because he texted me…

00:04:00.115 --> 00:04:01.700
that we were filed.

00:04:02.492 --> 00:04:03.410
He texted you?

00:04:06.455 --> 00:04:08.498
45 minutes later
the world knew.

00:04:08.582 --> 00:04:10.083
He just blind sighted you?

00:04:11.793 --> 00:04:14.796
Because of the crazy way
in which this went down,

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:16.256
people want answers.

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:21.261
And I fucking want answers.

00:04:22.387 --> 00:04:25.516
That's shitty.
Like beyond shitty.

00:04:27.142 --> 00:04:28.435
I know people
are saying like,

00:04:28.519 --> 00:04:30.354
we were only married
two years, but it's like,

00:04:30.437 --> 00:04:32.231
we were together
for six years.

00:04:32.314 --> 00:04:33.899
You deserve
more respect than that.

00:04:33.982 --> 00:04:37.069
I'm good
not being friends with you.

00:04:37.152 --> 00:04:40.614
It's been a very toxic
relationship

00:04:40.697 --> 00:04:41.823
having you in my life

00:04:41.907 --> 00:04:43.492
and so many times

00:04:43.575 --> 00:04:45.994
you've brought
toxic energy to me.

00:04:46.078 --> 00:04:48.205
And so I don't want anything
to do with that.

00:04:48.288 --> 00:04:50.082
Are you saying that you
will not give me a chance

00:04:50.165 --> 00:04:51.375
to be your friend?

00:04:51.458 --> 00:04:52.501
It looks like
it's going well.

00:04:52.584 --> 00:04:53.877
One of them
is gonna finish in the pool.

00:04:54.670 --> 00:04:56.672
No, I think actually--

00:04:56.755 --> 00:04:58.507
-I have a good feeling.
-I've seen some laughing.

00:04:58.590 --> 00:04:59.716
It's been a bit--

00:05:01.802 --> 00:05:03.595
Every time I deal with you,

00:05:03.679 --> 00:05:07.182
you do something insanely,
ridiculously hurtful

00:05:07.266 --> 00:05:09.560
like telling all the girls
not to like my Instagram's.

00:05:09.643 --> 00:05:12.104
Like, when you had a party

00:05:12.187 --> 00:05:14.523
and you made fun of me
on the drink list

00:05:14.606 --> 00:05:16.692
to 100's of your guests.

00:05:16.775 --> 00:05:19.444
She named a drink
"The Two-Face Chrishell."

00:05:20.988 --> 00:05:21.905
Okay,
you know what actually,

00:05:21.989 --> 00:05:23.866
it's "Chrishell's
Two Faced Tonic."

00:05:23.949 --> 00:05:24.783
I'm sorry.

00:05:24.867 --> 00:05:26.493
You know I actually do have
two faces for her

00:05:26.577 --> 00:05:28.537
I have to say,
because I don't like her

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:32.332
so I'm trying
to be professional and,

00:05:32.416 --> 00:05:34.793
so this is probably
the face that I give her.

00:05:36.879 --> 00:05:38.380
Do I look dead
behind the eyes?

00:05:38.463 --> 00:05:40.924
Because
you had a party prior

00:05:41.008 --> 00:05:42.134
and didn't invite me.

00:05:42.217 --> 00:05:43.468
I didn't have a party prior.

00:05:43.552 --> 00:05:45.554
You had a party prior
and you didn't invite me.

00:05:45.637 --> 00:05:47.556
Christine, we had parties
on the same night.

00:05:47.639 --> 00:05:50.184
But I didn't put your face
on a drink list

00:05:50.267 --> 00:05:52.186
and made fun
of you to all of my guests.

00:05:52.269 --> 00:05:53.937
To me in saying

00:05:54.021 --> 00:05:55.689
that you could do
all of this crazy behaviour

00:05:55.772 --> 00:05:57.524
and then sit here and
act like nothing happened.

00:05:57.608 --> 00:05:59.234
This is my olive branch.

00:05:59.318 --> 00:06:00.736
I've reached out many times.

00:06:00.819 --> 00:06:03.280
I do appreciate the apology.

00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:04.573
It's more
than I was expecting.

00:06:05.365 --> 00:06:07.159
What do they say,
keep your friends close,

00:06:07.242 --> 00:06:08.285
keep your enemies closer?

00:06:08.368 --> 00:06:09.536
Hey baby, how's it going?

00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:13.207
That's never been truer
than with Christine.

